03b4fc-eeae-5c86-9a52-755b32646d64" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287289 1145 "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=3$ and $b=5.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a semi-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the elipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/6db43ff41344f292c8cb5805febd175088fe068fe89927bade0c6fc2246c8781.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\pi ]$, we get the semi-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the semi-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287291 13194139534419 true] [17592186287290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287292 13194139534419 true] [17592186287290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287293 13194139534419 true] [17592186287290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287294 13194139534419 true] [17592186287290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287295 13194139534419 true] [17592186287290 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534419 true] [17592186287290 1041 "selection" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287290 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287292 13194139534419 true] [17592186287290 1110 #uuid "9fc3cf9b-cb13-50c7-b8c9-940fb76a2b2d" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287291 1034 "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287291 1111 #uuid "861da652-f677-5fa7-a40e-7ee0a493bbb4" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287292 1034 "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287292 1111 #uuid "1f83c84e-621b-5000-b60c-556777725315" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287293 1034 "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,2\\pi ]" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287293 1111 #uuid "df45a23e-d530-5666-a794-d534c05bcf4e" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287294 1034 "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287294 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287294 1111 #uuid "ba900f3f-81f4-5508-8e8f-09127ffabd6a" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287295 1034 "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287295 1111 #uuid "cb7df34a-a9ab-5f79-95ae-9b8e42fb067d" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287296 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287297 13194139534419 true] [17592186287296 1089 "q-106407" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287296 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534419 true] [17592186287296 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287296 1113 #uuid "7941ba73-b675-55db-8dee-437c04c038dc" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287296 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2}=1.\n$$" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287298 13194139534419 true] [17592186287297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287299 13194139534419 true] [17592186287297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287300 13194139534419 true] [17592186287297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287301 13194139534419 true] [17592186287297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287302 13194139534419 true] [17592186287297 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534419 true] [17592186287297 1041 "selection" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287297 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287299 13194139534419 true] [17592186287297 1110 #uuid "66be5f75-3750-5b2a-91d3-97d8cbea781f" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287298 1034 "\\frac{4}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{2}=1" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287298 1111 #uuid "9b97717b-207a-5230-beb9-93355c6929ba" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287299 1034 "\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2}=1" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287299 1111 #uuid "10ac0c76-3f15-5abf-8829-dc036d6014f7" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287300 1034 "\\frac{4}{9}{x}^{2}+\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{2}=1" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287300 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287300 1111 #uuid "bab6906c-7b2f-5240-b80e-f761bebd5185" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287301 1034 "\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2}=1" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287301 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287301 1111 #uuid "5fa7b105-beb5-5881-9e00-eabfc40f9f73" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287302 1034 "\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{2}=1" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287302 1111 #uuid "4bcee4d7-529d-5168-917d-18ba934e8ec5" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287303 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287304 13194139534419 true] [17592186287303 1089 "q-106408" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287303 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534419 true] [17592186287303 1100 "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287303 1113 #uuid "f3b7c704-e0a2-540d-961e-1826d160ef02" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287303 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2 \\\\ x-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2(x-2) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4{(x-2)}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3 \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2(y-3) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4{(y-3)}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-2)}^{2}+4{(y-3)}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n4{(x-2)}^{2}+4{(y-3)}^{2}=1.\n$$" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287304 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287305 13194139534419 true] [17592186287304 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287306 1319413953441