 17592186045465 13194139534419 true] [17592186287324 1100 "Determine the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287324 1113 #uuid "7d1ca52f-f1d5-56ec-b9ff-ecb0b7331355" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287324 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287325 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287326 13194139534419 true] [17592186287325 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287327 13194139534419 true] [17592186287325 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287328 13194139534419 true] [17592186287325 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287329 13194139534419 true] [17592186287325 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287330 13194139534419 true] [17592186287325 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534419 true] [17592186287325 1041 "selection" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287325 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287326 13194139534419 true] [17592186287325 1110