gned}x & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{6} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287332 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287333 13194139534419 true] [17592186287332 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287334 13194139534419 true] [17592186287332 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287335 13194139534419 true] [17592186287332 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287336 13194139534419 true] [17592186287332 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287337 13194139534419 true] [17592186287332 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534419 true] [17592186287332 1041 "selection" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287332 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287333 13194139534419 true] [17592186287332 1110 #uuid "ad1b808d-be7f-533e-807d-3c989cce7046" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287333 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287333 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287333 1111 #uuid "0ad88058-c875-5036-b4ea-3628069695fc" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287334 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287334 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534419 true] [17592186287334 1111 #uuid "aeb03b3c-e66b-5556-847f-39b8e859dc0b" 13194139534419 true] [17592186287335 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{{x}^{